WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.824 --> 00:00:01.946
(high pitched music)

00:00:01.946 --> 00:00:04.371
- [Ken] I always thought,
you know, a snow shoe

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:06.039
would really make a great cello.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:10.545
A wooden chair back
makes a cool guitar body.

00:00:10.545 --> 00:00:13.043
It turns out that one of my most playable

00:00:13.043 --> 00:00:15.463
instruments is a golf club.

00:00:15.463 --> 00:00:17.299
I'm seeing that transformative

00:00:17.299 --> 00:00:19.966
quality in my head all the time.

00:00:21.139 --> 00:00:23.400
What can I say, I'm attracted to trash.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.567
I don't know why.
(pleasant music)

00:00:28.965 --> 00:00:31.217
- [Narrator] Check out the
Jimi Hendrix of shovels.

00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:33.637
- [Narrator] It's a guitar
made up of lots of junk.

00:00:33.637 --> 00:00:36.107
- He even plays his zipper, from Brooklyn,

00:00:36.107 --> 00:00:38.198
New York, please welcome Ken Butler.

00:00:38.198 --> 00:00:39.198
(applause)

00:00:39.198 --> 00:00:41.742
- My name is Ken Butler,
I'm an artist and musician

00:00:41.742 --> 00:00:45.909
and known for building my
own experimental instruments.

00:00:47.366 --> 00:00:51.533
Since 1978, I think I've
made around 400 instruments.

00:00:53.831 --> 00:00:56.379
This whole thing started
for me when I was in

00:00:56.379 --> 00:01:00.546
my basement in Portland,
Oregon and I saw a rusty old

00:01:01.397 --> 00:01:05.745
beat up hatchet, put two strings
and two tuning pegs on it,

00:01:05.745 --> 00:01:10.003
plugged it into my guitar
amp and was quite stunned

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.509
that it actually sounded
like a horrible violin.

00:01:12.509 --> 00:01:14.564
(violin music)

00:01:14.564 --> 00:01:16.565
The ax violin was the first time that

00:01:16.565 --> 00:01:19.315
somebody said that's a cool idea.

00:01:22.235 --> 00:01:24.866
If I go walking around the neighborhood,

00:01:24.866 --> 00:01:26.534
everywhere you look, you see such

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:30.288
amazing conglomerations
of potential sculpture.

00:01:30.288 --> 00:01:32.874
There's crutches, tennis
rackets, parts of furniture,

00:01:32.874 --> 00:01:35.541
boom, I'm right there with that.

00:01:36.671 --> 00:01:39.167
Ya know, when I build
stringed instruments,

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:42.083
really just need three things,

00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:44.750
the head, the neck and the body.

00:01:47.221 --> 00:01:51.388
A spoon has that parameter,
a key looks like a guitar.

00:01:53.355 --> 00:01:56.566
It has the, you know, and then
there's the little body.

00:01:56.566 --> 00:02:00.446
This is from a very inexpensive mandolin.

00:02:00.446 --> 00:02:02.946
Of course some of the things become crazy

00:02:02.946 --> 00:02:06.738
Baruch Asambleas of
multiple, multiple necks.

00:02:06.738 --> 00:02:10.078
It's ridiculous but that's how it works.

00:02:10.078 --> 00:02:14.249
My shovel guitar, I guess
it's a small snow shovel.

00:02:14.249 --> 00:02:16.335
It's just a quirky object and it sounds

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:19.965
unbelievably beautiful, the
qualities and characters

00:02:19.965 --> 00:02:23.089
that the golf club has is amazing.

00:02:23.089 --> 00:02:24.299
(string music)

00:02:24.299 --> 00:02:26.381
There's one that's made
from a beach paddle

00:02:26.381 --> 00:02:29.640
that has a ukulele neck and a cane.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:33.014
(string music)

00:02:33.014 --> 00:02:36.562
Sometimes people think my
intention is humor, it's not.

00:02:36.562 --> 00:02:38.938
I think it's surprising
to people that I can

00:02:38.938 --> 00:02:43.105
generate genuine emotion
and meaning and real music

00:02:44.856 --> 00:02:48.365
on something as ridiculous
as a hockey stick

00:02:48.365 --> 00:02:52.371
or a tennis racket or a broom
or a shovel or a golf club.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:55.917
At the real core of
what I'm doing, it's to

00:02:55.917 --> 00:02:58.377
communicate to other people
that the things right around

00:02:58.377 --> 00:03:02.544
them can be magical and
transformative and even spiritual.

00:03:03.465 --> 00:03:05.129
Who knows, if I hadn't found

00:03:05.129 --> 00:03:07.796
that ax, what would've happened.

00:03:11.427 --> 00:03:14.510
(high pitched music)

